# TODO - Deterministic cross-backend artifact hashing

## Objective

Require byte-identical outputs and hashes across backends for declared
deterministic workloads, including versioned example artifacts and compiler-
produced `.malbolge` artifacts where deterministic builds are promised.

## Acceptance

- Identical declared source/profile, compiler version, selected algorithm,
  seed, configuration and backend policy reproduce byte-identical output or
  an explicitly specified canonical form. Different valid optimizers/CPU/CUDA
  proposal orders may emit different bytes; each artifact carries its own hash
  and independently checked semantic equivalence to the same source IR.
- Cross-backend fixtures distinguish deterministic replay from equivalent
  but nonidentical artifacts and reject a semantically divergent candidate.
- The end-to-end fixture demonstrates the intended behavior from admitted
  source/input through the actual generated/executed Malbolge path.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `docs/technical/examples/`,
  `tests/applications/`, `benchmarks/applications/`, `runtime/`.
- Required evidence: reproducible build/run commands, expected outputs or
  interaction traces, artifact hashes, and end-to-end verification.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `malbolge-layout-and-encoding-backend`,
  `differential-vm-verification`.
